      "text": "Over the long run, yes. Over the last year, no. Reddit (RDDT) is still up about 3x since its IPO, but the chart has been falling for about a year and is now drifting sideways with no clear direction.\n\n**From the IPO to today (March 2024 \u2013 September 2026)**\n- First-day close: **$50.44**. The IPO priced at $34, which comes from my own knowledge, not this data. Last close: **$149.84**. That's about +197% from the first close, or roughly 4.4x the IPO price.\n- The low came early, around $37 in April 2024. The stock then more than doubled on the October 2024 earnings gap (about $82 to $116).\n- The run peaked near **$283 in September 2025**.\n\n**The last year: lower highs**\n- After that peak, each rally stopped lower than the one before: about $263 in early 2026, about $208 mid-year and about $184 more recently.\n- It bottomed around **$120** this spring, rallied to about $200, then gapped down about 21% in late summer (about $178 to $141).\n- It's now about **47% below its high**, stuck roughly between $140 and $165.\n\n**Current indicators (as of September 25, 2026)**\n| Indicator | Reading | Read |\n|---|---|---|\n| Trend (ADX 9) | Very weak | No real trend, just chop |\n| RSI (14) | 44.7 | Slightly weak, neither overbought nor oversold |\n| MACD | Barely above its signal line (+0.05) | Downside momentum is fading, but nothing confirmed yet |\n| Stochastic | 31 and falling | Weak |\n| Bollinger Bands | Price below the middle band ($153.76) | Mildly bearish |\n| Volume | 0.55x average | Low conviction either way |\n\nThe analysis tool's overall rating is \"strongly bearish.\" Given how weak the trend reading is, I'd call it neutral-to-bearish consolidation rather than an active selloff.\n\n**Price levels to watch**\n- **Support:** $142\u2013143, then about $135. A close below about $135 would open the way back toward the $120s spring low.\n- **Resistance:** about $157, then about $165, then about $184. A move above $165\u2013184 on strong volume would be the first sign the downtrend of lower highs is over.\n\n**Bottom line:** IPO buyers are still well ahead, but the chart isn't bullish right now. It's been falling since September 2025 and is now moving sideways. A bullish case would need a break above the mid-$160s, and ideally above $184.\n\nThis is technical analysis only, not investment advice. I can also run a support/resistance check, a market regime analysis or a strategy backtest on RDDT if that would help."
